// **The crop a colony farms** (`src/sim/garden.rs`, the plants-and-ants lane,
// 2026-10-30). Scott's repo review found plants and ants barely touch: a leaf
// an ant cut was worth 40 J and nothing else, so nothing gave a colony a
// reason to keep plants near home. Plant matter the ants carry home and leave
// lying in the dark nest -- cut leaf, dead leaf, litter, grass, flowers,
// crumbs (`garden_fodder`) -- turns into this, spreads through the pile, and
// ripens while it stays dark: a room the colony stocks with leaves becomes a
// pale garden it eats from in a famine.
//
// **Its worth is in `aux` (`carries_worth`)**, as crumbs' is, because the
// garden ripens it cell by cell: young fungus is worth what the fodder was,
// and every garden visit in the dark adds to it up to `garden::RIPE_WORTH`.
// `food_energy` below is only the fallback for a bare cell.
//
// **The shade is the ripeness** (`garden::shade_for`): the palette runs from
// a dull grey-green, just started, to a bright pale mint, ripe, so a player
// sees a garden coming on without an overlay. **Mint, not the cream of a real
// fungus garden**, found from the first picture: cream is the colour of the
// brood pile (`brood.ron`) that sits in the same rooms, and the two read as
// one blob.
//
// **It does not roll**, for crumbs' reason: a garden on a tunnel floor must
// not slide down the shaft and pack it. It still drops straight down through
// open air.
(
    name: "fungus",
    display: "Fungus garden",
    kind: Powder,
    density: 0.6,
    friction_angle: 40.0,
    colors: [
        (92, 118, 108),
        (112, 156, 140),
        (140, 196, 176),
        (178, 232, 210),
    ],
    flammability: 0.2,
    burn_temperature: 480.0,
    burn_duration: 30,
    burns_into: "ash",
    heat_conductivity: 0.2,
    insubstantial: true,
    falls_through_organisms: true,
    food_energy: 120.0,
    carries_worth: true,
    rolls: false,
    penetration_resistance: 0.2,
    food_class: -1.0,
)
